-- chem/freespace.cub — the free energy's local bracket with patches in space, on the HP model of chem/selection.cub
-- (6 residues on the square lattice, first step fixed). The site formulation: every lattice site carries a residue
-- index or nothing. Its constraints of radius one are kept whole: residue 0 only at the origin and residue 1 only at
-- its fixed neighbour; a site carrying residue i ≥ 2 has a neighbour carrying i − 1; a site carrying i ≤ 4 has a
-- neighbour carrying i + 1; and the weight is x for every pair of neighbouring sites carrying H residues at (0,3),
-- (0,5), (1,4) or (2,5). The one constraint that is not local in space, each residue exactly once, is kept only
-- inside patches of r × r sites: a residue index occurs at most once in each patch, that is, two sites with the same
-- index are at Chebyshev distance at least r. Every walk is such a labelling, so Z_r ≥ Z. For r ≥ 3 it is exact: two
-- neighbours of one site are at Chebyshev distance at most 2, so no site has two successors, every index occurs once
-- (by induction from residue 1), and the labelling is a self-avoiding walk. At r = 2 a site may have its two opposite
-- neighbours carry the next index, and the labellings are branched. Evaluation: the labellings are listed layer by
-- layer (the sites of index i from those of index i − 1), each with its numbers of the four kinds of contact; this
-- is a search of the relaxation's feasible set, not a transfer matrix across rows, which would be the local
-- algorithm. The reference Z is chem/freedual.cub's `fd-ref` from the enumeration of walks.
import "freedual.hypercubical"

